    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 the full suite reports **58 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp46Tests`.\n\nHere's what I changed to implement soft-delete for owners:\n\n**Model & schema** \u2014 added a persisted `deleted` boolean:\n- `Owner.java`: new `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`; primitive `boolean` defaults to false, so a newly created owner is not deleted.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`: added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to the `owners` table (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema had to be updated explicitly; the `DEFAULT FALSE` keeps existing seed inserts valid).\n- `openapi.yml`: added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field, which MapStruct maps automatically by name \u2014 that's what surfaces `$.deleted` on `GET`.\n\n**Behavior**:\n- `DeleteOwner.java`: now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner (retaining the row) instead of `delete`ing it. The `DELETE` pipeline still responds 204 (2xx), and `GET` still returns the owner afterward with `deleted` true.\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity`, `EnsureUniqueHousehold`, and `AssignPossibleDuplicate`: each now skips existing owners flagged `deleted` when scanning `findAll()`, so a soft-deleted owner no longer blocks (or soft-flags) a re-creation.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests confirm both the flag/retain behavior and that a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.",
